   "model": "I agree that some advertising needs tighter control, but not a full ban. False claims and ads aimed at children are clearly harmful: young people cannot judge a message that tells them happiness comes in a box. Rules against deception protect the weak and keep markets fair. At the same time, adults are allowed to be persuaded; banning all advertising would limit free choice and hurt small firms that rely on it to be seen. The right balance is to ban lies and child-targeted pressure, while letting honest comparison compete. That way we keep information flowing without letting tricks decide what we buy.",
