   "model": "I partly agree that voluntary work has value for young people, but tying it to graduation is a step too far. On the plus side, helping others builds empathy, routine, and a sense of civic duty that exams rarely teach. Some pupils discover a calling through it. Yet a hard requirement punishes those who work after school to support their family; for them it becomes one more hurdle, not a gift. A better model is to offer it richly and count it lightly — extra credit, not a gate. Encourage the habit, reward the heart, but let the unwilling opt out. Forced kindness is still better than none, yet choice is what makes it mean something.",
