   "model": "I partly agree that social media divides more than it informs, because the design rewards outrage over nuance. Algorithms feed us voices we already like, building echo chambers where the other side looks strange and wrong. That breeds division and makes real debate rarer. Yet the same tools also put more information in more hands than any paper ever did; a curious user can hear many sides in a night. The outcome hinges on habit, not the platform alone: follow broadly, check sources, and step out of the chamber. Used lazily, social media splits us; used wisely, it can inform us. The feed follows the user.",
