   "model": "I disagree that small talk is a waste, though I understand the busy-world impulse to skip it. Those few light minutes build the trust that later makes teamwork, deals, and friendships possible; many opportunities start with a hello, not a pitch. Dismissing it as filler risks seeming cold and misses the human signal that says 'I'm safe to approach'. That said, fake or endless chatter is indeed a drain, so the art is to keep it brief and genuine — a real question, a real laugh, then move on. Small talk is not the meeting; it is the handshake before it. Spend a little, and the rest goes smoother. Cut it fully, and you cut the thread.",
