   "model": "I disagree that the next fifty years must be worse, though the risks are real and loud. Climate pressure and job churn are genuine; ignoring them would be foolish. Yet the same era brings longer, healthier lives, tools that spread knowledge instantly, and a generation more aware of the planet than any before. Whether the balance tips bad or good depends less on fate than on choices made now — on energy, on fairness, on whether we adapt in time. The future is not a verdict handed down; it is a draft we keep editing. Prepare, vote, and build, and the coming decades can surpass the last. Fear warns; it should not write the story.",
