   "text": "Social media promises connection, yet many users feel more isolated than ever. The problem is not the tool but how we use it. We scroll through a highlight reel of other people's lives and quietly compare, forgetting that we see only their best moments.\n\nEach like delivers a small dopamine hit, training us to seek validation from strangers. Over time, constant comparison erodes self-worth. We resent lives that look easier, not realising they are curated, not complete.\n\nThe answer is not to delete everything. Moderation works. Set limits, follow accounts that help rather than hurt, and post more authentically. A short detox now and then resets the habit. Remember: the feed is a selection, not a truth. Your ordinary Tuesday is someone's secret goal.",
