   "words": 252,
   "text": "Money is not only maths; it is story. The same salary feels like freedom to one person and never enough to another. Our habits were written early—by what we saw at home, by scares we lived through—and they run on long after the facts change.\n\nTwo errors recur. One is impulse: buying to soothe a feeling that spending cannot fix. The other is never feeling sufficient, chasing a number that moves as we approach it. Both breed anxiety rather than security.\n\nThe quieter path is behavioural. Pay your future self first; let savings compound while you sleep. Be frugal by choice, not shame. Know what 'enough' means to you, and resist the neighbour's scoreboard. A windfall feels like a reset, but without a plan it leaks away.\n\nWealth, then, is less about income than about a calm relationship with enough.",
