   "text": "Sixty days ago, the plan was small: one step, repeated. Today that repetition is a milestone worth naming. Language learning, like most worth-having things, is not a sprint but a climb you stop noticing—until you look back and see the height gained.\n\nThe gains are cumulative and quiet. A larger vocabulary, a steadier ear, a calmer approach to mistakes. Some days plateaued; that is normal. Consistency, not brilliance, carried you through the flat weeks. The reward was never a certificate but a slightly wider self.\n\nSustaining momentum now matters more than celebrating. Set a gentle intention for the next stretch: keep the streak, but kindly. Reflect honestly, adjust when stuck, and carry the habit forward without forcing perfection.\n\nOnward, then. The next sixty days need no grand plan—only the same small step, taken again, because you already know it works.",
