  "writing": {
   "prompt": "In many professions, people now work alongside intelligent software. What are the benefits of this, and what problems might it cause?",
   "outline": [
    "引言：说明人机协作已在多行业出现，将谈收益与风险",
    "主体1：收益 — 减少重复劳动、提高一致性与速度、让专业人员专注复杂判断",
    "主体2：问题 — 过度信任导致失察、技能退化、责任归属模糊",
    "结论：按长处分工、保留人工最终决定与持续训练"
   ],
   "model": "In fields ranging from medicine to law, professionals increasingly work alongside software that analyses information for them. This partnership brings clear gains, although it also introduces risks that organisations must manage.\n\nThe benefits are mainly practical. Software handles repetitive, high-volume tasks without becoming tired, which allows specialists to spend their time on complex cases. In hospitals, for example, a system that reviews scans overnight can reduce a radiologist's workload substantially and highlight problems that a tired reader might overlook. Consistency also improves, since the same standard is applied to every case.\n\nProblems arise, however, when confidence becomes automatic. Research on automated systems shows that operators who see correct results repeatedly stop examining them carefully, and therefore miss the rare serious error. There is a further concern about skills: if junior staff never perform routine analysis themselves, they may never develop the judgement needed later. Responsibility can also become unclear when nobody is certain who made a decision.\n\nIn my view these problems are manageable through design and training. Systems should show their reasoning and indicate uncertainty, professionals should retain the final decision, and organisations must ensure that people continue to practise the skills the software performs.",
   "checklist": [
    "是否分别回答了收益与问题",
    "并列与从属连词是否使用正确(无 because...so 并用)",
    "是否提到技能退化与责任归属这两个较深入的问题",
    "是否使用 judgement / oversight / expertise 等本课词汇",
    "结论是否给出设计与培训两方面的对策"
   ]
  },
  "out": "今天讲人机协作，分工原则是：重复、量大、可测量的交给机器，需要语境、伦理与责任的留给人。最大风险不是机器叛变而是人过度顺从。语法练连词，牢记 because 与 so、although 与 but 在英文中只能留一个。"
