  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe everyone should spend regular periods without any digital devices. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "引言：说明设备无处不在，表明基本同意但反对极端做法",
    "主体1：支持理由 — 恢复注意力、无聊带来创造力、改善睡眠与人际在场感",
    "主体2：限度与让步 — 部分工作与照护需随时在线、彻底断网不现实",
    "结论：主张定时而非长期断开，重点在习惯而非设备"
   ],
   "model": "It is often suggested that people should regularly spend time completely without digital devices. I agree with this proposal in principle, although I think short and regular breaks are more realistic than long periods of disconnection.\n\nThere are convincing reasons to switch off. Attention recovers slowly after interruption, so uninterrupted hours allow deeper thinking than a whole day of fragmented work. Periods of boredom, which have almost disappeared, are also valuable, since a wandering mind produces ideas that concentrated effort cannot. Eating or walking without a phone visibly improves conversation and sleep as well.\n\nThere are, however, practical limits. Many employees must remain reachable, and people caring for children or elderly relatives cannot responsibly disappear for a weekend. For those living far from family, a device is the main link to the people they love, so removing it would increase isolation rather than reduce it.\n\nMy conclusion is that the aim should be regular rather than total disconnection. A few device-free hours each week, a phone left in another room during meals and one walk without headphones would deliver most of the benefit. It is the habit of constant checking, not the technology itself, that needs to change.",
   "checklist": [
    "是否表明同意程度并说明限制条件",
    "强调句 It is ... that 是否至少使用一次",
    "全篇时态是否一致且无间接引语错误",
    "是否使用 unplug / boredom / moderation 等本课词汇",
    "结论是否落在习惯而非设备本身"
   ]
  },
  "out": "第90天收尾，也是整册的总结：问题不在屏幕，而在没有任何一件事明确不是屏幕。三条可执行建议：每周留几小时无设备、吃饭时手机放另一个房间、每周一次不戴耳机的散步。语法上复习强调句 It is ... that 和全篇时态一致，把前29天的定语从句、条件句、被动语态一并回顾。"
