   "text": "A: Could you look at my resume before I send it?\nB: Sure. How long is it?\nA: Three pages. I listed every job since university.\nB: That is the first problem. Two pages maximum, one is better.\nA: But I do not want to lose anything important.\nB: Then ask what is relevant. They want a project manager, not a waiter.\nA: Fair. So I cut the cafe job?\nB: Cut the details, keep one line if you need the dates.\nA: What about this part, \"responsible for the team blog\"?\nB: Weak. How many posts? Did readers increase?\nA: We went from about two hundred to a thousand readers.\nB: Write that. Numbers survive a ten-second read.\nA: I never think of my work in numbers.\nB: Most people do not. That is why numbers stand out.\nA: Anything else?\nB: Proofread it twice, then send it to me again.\nA: Thanks. I will rewrite it tonight.\nB: Good. And change the layout, it looks crowded.",
