   "text": "A: I worked until eight again yesterday.\nB: What did you actually finish?\nA: Emails, mostly. And two meetings.\nB: So the client proposal is still waiting.\nA: Do not remind me. I keep putting it off.\nB: When do you feel sharpest during the day?\nA: Early. Before nine I think clearly.\nB: Then you should give that hour to the proposal, not the inbox.\nA: People expect a fast reply though.\nB: Do they, or do you assume it? Try answering at eleven for a week.\nA: That is fair. Nobody has ever complained.\nB: And how long do you think the proposal needs?\nA: About two hours.\nB: Then block three. You always underestimate.\nA: True. Last time it took a whole day.\nB: Write that down. Real numbers fix bad plans.\nA: Okay, tomorrow morning, phone in the drawer.\nB: You had better tell your team, or they will interrupt you.",
