   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，给出立场（同意平衡更重要，但需承认收入的基础作用）",
    "主体一：健康与人际关系是长期价值，过劳导致效率下降与职业倦怠",
    "主体二：一定收入是安全感的前提，低薪同样带来压力",
    "结论：收入需达到可接受水平之后，时间与健康的边际价值更高"
   ],
   "model": "People often have to choose between a demanding job that pays well and a quieter one that leaves time for family. In my view, balance matters more, although a reasonable income is still necessary.\n\nThe first reason is health. Employees who work sixty hours a week sleep badly, exercise less and eventually become less productive, so the extra hours buy very little. Relationships suffer too, and no salary can replace the years a parent misses at home.\n\nOn the other hand, financial worry is its own kind of stress. Someone who cannot pay rent will not enjoy free afternoons, and low pay often forces people into second jobs, which destroys the balance they wanted.\n\nI would therefore argue that money matters up to a certain point. Once a salary covers housing, food and modest savings, extra income adds far less to happiness than an extra evening with friends. Companies should recognise this and compete with reasonable hours as well as with pay.",
