   "text": "A: I have to present to forty people on Thursday.\nB: How do you feel about it?\nA: Honestly, terrified. My hands always shake.\nB: Everyone's do. Have you rehearsed out loud?\nA: I read the slides in my head.\nB: That is not rehearsing. Stand up and say it properly.\nA: It feels silly alone in a room.\nB: It feels sillier when you dry up on stage.\nA: Fair point. How many times?\nB: The first minute, ten times. The rest, twice.\nA: Why the first minute?\nB: Because once it is automatic, your body calms down.\nA: I have twenty-two slides.\nB: Cut it to six. What are your three main ideas?\nA: Cost, timeline and risk.\nB: Then two slides each. Delete the rest.\nA: And if I forget something?\nB: Pause. A pause sounds confident, not lost.",
