   "text": "A: Our group project is a mess.\nB: What is going wrong?\nA: Nobody knows who is doing what.\nB: Did you assign owners for each part?\nA: We said we would all do the research together.\nB: There is your problem. Shared tasks disappear.\nA: But we wanted it to feel equal.\nB: Equal workload, yes. Equal ownership, no. One name per task.\nA: Okay. Rosa could take the survey.\nB: Can she finish it by Friday?\nA: I think so. She is reliable.\nB: And who checks the final document?\nA: Nobody, so far. Maybe me.\nB: Then say it out loud in the group chat.\nA: There is another problem. Tom disagrees with everything.\nB: Is he disagreeing about ideas or about people?\nA: Ideas, mostly.\nB: That is useful. A team where nobody argues is usually hiding something.",
