   "text": "A: I am thinking about leaving my job.\nB: Are you unhappy, or just bored?\nA: Bored, I think. Nothing has changed in three years.\nB: What are you going to do instead?\nA: That is the problem. I have no idea.\nB: Then do not resign yet. What parts of the week do you enjoy?\nA: The client meetings. And writing the monthly analysis.\nB: And what do you avoid?\nA: Anything with spreadsheets. I put it off for days.\nB: So you want more contact with people and more writing.\nA: When you say it like that, it sounds obvious.\nB: Which jobs involve both?\nA: Account management, maybe. Or research communication.\nB: Good. Talk to two people in each before you apply.\nA: I am meeting an old colleague on Thursday, actually.\nB: Perfect. Ask what she does on a bad day, not a good one.\nA: Why a bad day?\nB: Because that is the part you will live with.",
