  "speaking": {
   "card": "Describe a time when a message or instruction was misunderstood. You should say: what the message was; who was involved; what went wrong; and explain how the misunderstanding was resolved.",
   "part3": "Why do emails cause more conflict than phone calls? / Should companies limit the number of internal messages? / Is direct communication always better than polite indirect language? / How does communication change between different generations at work?",
   "useful": "Just to clarify, do you mean / Correct me if I am wrong, but / To summarise what we agreed / Could you confirm the deadline / I will follow up on that"
  },
  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that face-to-face communication at work is always better than communication by email or message. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，立场为部分同意，取决于沟通目的",
    "主体一：面对面的优势——语气、表情、即时澄清、处理敏感话题",
    "主体二：书面沟通的优势——留痕、异步、跨时区、便于复杂数据",
    "结论：按内容选择渠道，敏感用面谈，事实与决定用书面"
   ],
   "model": "With teams now spread across countries, many managers argue that nothing replaces a real conversation. I agree that face-to-face communication is superior for some purposes, but not for all.\n\nSpeaking in person clearly helps when a topic is sensitive or complex. Facial expression and tone reveal doubt or discomfort that a written message hides, and misunderstandings can be corrected within seconds rather than over three days of email. Difficult subjects such as criticism, disagreement or bad news should therefore be handled in person or at least by phone.\n\nWritten communication, however, has advantages that speech cannot match. It creates a record, so nobody argues later about what was agreed, and it allows colleagues in different time zones to work without waiting. Detailed figures and instructions are also far easier to check on a screen than to remember from a meeting.\n\nIn conclusion, the channel should follow the message. I believe organisations should encourage staff to discuss sensitive issues face to face, while continuing to confirm facts, decisions and deadlines in short written summaries.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 立场部分同意，开头即明确",
    "✔ 两段各自论证并有例子（criticism / time zones）",
    "✔ 使用间接引语或转述结构至少一次",
    "✔ 连接词多样（however / therefore / in conclusion）",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论提出操作建议"
   ]
  },
