  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some employers now use personality tests and computer programs to select staff instead of traditional interviews. Do the advantages of this development outweigh the disadvantages?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，说明趋势并预告判断（弊大于利/需谨慎）",
    "主体一：优点——效率高、可处理大量申请、减少某些主观偏见",
    "主体二：缺点——算法沿袭历史偏见、忽视沟通与潜力、缺乏透明度",
    "结论：可作初筛工具，但最终决定应由人做出"
   ],
   "model": "Large employers increasingly use automated tests and software to sort applications before any human sees them. Although this saves time, I believe the disadvantages currently outweigh the benefits.\n\nThe advantages are practical. A popular company may receive thousands of applications, and software can process them in hours, applying the same criteria to everyone. Supporters also argue that machines ignore a candidate's accent or appearance, which may reduce certain forms of prejudice.\n\nNevertheless, these systems have serious weaknesses. Algorithms are trained on past hiring decisions, so any bias that existed before is repeated and given the appearance of science. Qualities that matter most in real work, such as judgement, warmth and the ability to explain a difficult idea, are extremely hard to measure in a test. Rejected candidates are also given no explanation, which feels unfair and damages the employer's reputation.\n\nIn my opinion, automated tools should be used only for the earliest stage of selection, to check basic requirements. The final decision should be made by people who can meet the candidate and take responsibility for the choice.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 明确回答 advantages / disadvantages 的比较",
    "✔ 优缺点各一段，论据具体（算法偏见、无反馈）",
    "✔ 至少三处正确使用被动语态",
    "✔ 使用 nevertheless / in my opinion 等衔接",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论给出限定条件"
   ]
  },
