  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that the best way to learn something is to teach it to others. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，立场为基本同意但需前提",
    "主体一：教学迫使组织信息、预判提问，暴露知识漏洞",
    "主体二：局限——初学者可能教错、需先有基础输入",
    "结论：教是极佳的检验与巩固手段，但不能替代最初的学习阶段"
   ],
   "model": "It is often claimed that nobody understands a subject until they have taught it. I largely agree with this idea, although teaching cannot replace every stage of learning.\n\nExplaining material to someone else is a demanding test. The teacher must organise the information logically, choose examples and answer unexpected questions, and any weak point becomes obvious immediately. Silent rereading allows a student to skim over difficulties, whereas a listener who says \"I do not follow\" forces the explanation to be repaired. This is why many students report that they finally understood a topic during revision with a friend.\n\nTeaching alone, however, has clear limits. A beginner who explains a subject too early may pass on mistakes with great confidence, and complex fields require careful reading and practice before any explanation is possible. Teaching tests knowledge; it does not create it from nothing.\n\nIn my view, the sensible approach is to study a topic properly and then immediately try to explain it without notes. Used in this order, teaching becomes the most efficient way of turning fragile information into lasting understanding.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 立场 largely agree 并指出限制",
    "✔ 正反两面均有论证",
    "✔ 动名词与不定式使用正确（explaining / to explain）",
    "✔ 使用 whereas / however / in my view",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论有明确顺序建议"
   ]
  },
