   "text": "A: I have four hundred pages to read before Monday.\nB: All of it carefully?\nA: That was the plan. It is not going well.\nB: What do you actually need from it?\nA: The main arguments. There will be an essay question.\nB: Then you do not need every word. Skim the structure first.\nA: How?\nB: Introduction, first sentence of each paragraph, conclusion.\nA: That feels like cheating.\nB: It is faster and usually more effective for arguments.\nA: I normally highlight as I go.\nB: How much of your last book is yellow?\nA: Most of it, honestly.\nB: Then the highlighting told you nothing. Write one sentence per section instead.\nA: In my own words?\nB: Always. Copying is the least useful thing you can do.\nA: That will take longer today.\nB: And save you three days in revision week.",
