  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe that reading fiction is a waste of time compared with reading factual books. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，立场为不同意",
    "主体一：小说培养同理心与语言能力，提供事实类书籍无法给予的视角",
    "主体二：承认非虚构在专业知识与实用技能上的效率优势",
    "结论：两者功能不同，不应比较优劣，理想是兼读"
   ],
   "model": "Some readers regard novels as entertainment and prefer books that deliver facts. I disagree with this view, because fiction develops abilities that factual writing cannot.\n\nThe clearest benefit of fiction is understanding other people. Following a character's thoughts over three hundred pages allows a reader to experience decisions made under pressure in another country, class or century, and research suggests that regular novel readers are better at recognising emotion in others. Fiction is also the richest source of natural language, which is why many language learners progress faster with stories than with textbooks.\n\nI accept that non-fiction is more efficient for specific purposes. A student who needs to understand economics should read an economics book, and a manager preparing a presentation will not find the answer in a novel. Factual writing organises knowledge in a way that stories deliberately avoid.\n\nNevertheless, calling fiction a waste of time confuses usefulness with immediate application. The most valuable effects of reading, such as patience, empathy and a wider vocabulary, appear slowly. In my opinion, a serious reader needs both kinds of book.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 立场明确（disagree）并在开头点明",
    "✔ 有让步段承认非虚构的优势",
    "✔ 正确使用比较级与最高级（more efficient / the richest）",
    "✔ 使用 nevertheless / in my opinion 等衔接",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论回到题目"
   ]
  },
