   "text": "A: My lecture notes are twelve pages and I understand none of them.\nB: Twelve pages for one hour? You are transcribing.\nA: I am afraid of missing something.\nB: You are missing the thinking. Write keywords only.\nA: Then how do I remember the details?\nB: The slides have the details. Your notes should have the structure.\nA: What format do you use?\nB: Cornell. Content on the right, questions on the left, summary at the bottom.\nA: When do you write the questions?\nB: The same evening, which is the part everyone skips.\nA: How long does that take?\nB: Ten minutes. It roughly doubles what I remember.\nA: Do you type or write by hand?\nB: By hand in lectures, because I cannot keep up, so I have to choose.\nA: And afterwards?\nB: I type the summary, which makes it searchable later.\nA: That sounds like a system I could copy.\nB: Copy it for two weeks before you judge it.",
