   "text": "A: I sat at my desk for eight hours and produced nothing.\nB: How many times did you check your phone?\nA: I have no idea. A lot.\nB: That is the answer, then.\nA: But I only look for a second.\nB: The look costs a second. Getting back into the work costs minutes.\nA: I keep it face down, though.\nB: It still pulls at you. Put it in a drawer.\nA: That feels extreme.\nB: It is easier than resisting it four hundred times.\nA: How long should I work in one block?\nB: Try forty-five minutes with a clear stopping point.\nA: The first ten minutes are always horrible.\nB: They are for everyone. That part does not disappear, it gets shorter.\nA: So I just tolerate it?\nB: Yes. Boredom is part of the training now.\nA: And breaks?\nB: A short walk. Not a screen, or you start again from zero.",
