   "text": "A: This article says students who eat breakfast get better grades.\nB: Probably true. What does it conclude?\nA: That schools should provide free breakfast.\nB: That might be a good idea, but does the study prove it?\nA: It found a strong correlation.\nB: Correlation with what else, though? Who eats breakfast regularly?\nA: Children in organised households, I suppose.\nB: And those households may help with homework too.\nA: So the breakfast might not be the cause.\nB: It might be. But the study cannot show that.\nA: How would you test it properly?\nB: Give breakfast to one group, not to another, and compare.\nA: That sounds unfair to the second group.\nB: Which is why this research is difficult.\nA: I nearly shared the article without thinking.\nB: Most people do. Who funded the study, by the way?\nA: A cereal company. Oh.\nB: Even though the finding may be real, that matters.",
