  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe that university students should be required to teach or help younger students as part of their course. Do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，立场为同意但需自愿与培训",
    "主体一：对导生的好处——巩固知识、锻炼沟通与责任感",
    "主体二：对学弟学妹的好处——语言更贴近、氛围更轻松",
    "结论：建议设为可选学分项目并提供培训，而非强制"
   ],
   "model": "Several universities now ask senior students to run study sessions for those in earlier years. I believe such programmes are valuable, although making them compulsory would be a mistake.\n\nThe tutors benefit most. Preparing an explanation forces a student to reorganise the material and to notice steps that were never properly understood, and answering unexpected questions is far harder than passing an examination. Students who teach also develop communication skills that employers repeatedly say graduates lack.\n\nYounger students gain as well. A tutor who studied the same module recently explains in familiar language and remembers which parts caused difficulty, and beginners are usually less embarrassed to admit confusion to someone close to their own age than to a professor.\n\nNevertheless, teaching is a skill, and an unwilling or untrained tutor can spread misunderstandings confidently. For this reason I would let universities offer such schemes as optional credit, with short training and supervision. Voluntary participation would ensure that the people explaining actually want to be there, which is precisely what makes peer teaching work.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 立场 agree with condition 并说明",
    "✔ 分别论证对两方的益处",
    "✔ 使役动词使用正确（make / let / get sb to do）",
    "✔ 使用 nevertheless / for this reason",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论提出具体机制"
   ]
  },
