   "text": "A: That call was ninety minutes and we decided nothing.\nB: Was there an agenda?\nA: Not really. Someone said we would see where it goes.\nB: Then it must have gone nowhere.\nA: Fourteen people, and about four of them spoke.\nB: The others might have been working on something else.\nA: Almost certainly. I could hear typing.\nB: Who was chairing?\nA: Nobody officially. That was part of the problem.\nB: Someone has to. Otherwise the loudest voice decides.\nA: I did not want to interrupt.\nB: Online you sometimes have to. Or use the chat.\nA: What would you change for next week?\nB: Thirty minutes, five people, agenda sent the day before.\nA: People will say they are being excluded.\nB: Send them the minutes. Reading takes two minutes.\nA: And if a topic needs everyone?\nB: Then invite everyone, but name each person when you want an answer.",
