   "text": "A: I think I upset our Japanese colleague yesterday.\nB: What happened?\nA: I said his proposal would not work, in the meeting.\nB: In front of everyone?\nA: Yes. In Stockholm that is normal.\nB: It is normal in a lot of places. Just not everywhere.\nA: He said nothing at all.\nB: That silence probably meant something.\nA: So what should I have done?\nB: Asked a question instead. \"How would this handle the delay?\"\nA: That is softer, but it is still a challenge.\nB: Exactly. Same content, different packaging.\nA: Should I apologise now?\nB: Speak to him privately. Say you value his work.\nA: Will that be enough?\nB: Usually. And ask how he prefers to receive feedback.\nA: I assumed being direct was respectful.\nB: It is, where you come from. Here you meet people halfway.",
