   "text": "A: I want to move from teaching into corporate training, but I have no business experience.\nB: Have you not been training people for twelve years?\nA: Children, though. It is not the same.\nB: Some of it is not. Most of it is.\nA: Such as?\nB: Explaining difficult material. Managing a room. Designing a course.\nA: I never thought of a lesson plan as course design.\nB: It is exactly that, with a different name.\nA: They will still ask about business knowledge.\nB: Then learn the vocabulary. That takes weeks, not years.\nA: What should I put on my application?\nB: Numbers. How many people, how many hours, what improved.\nA: Two hundred students a year, and results rose by fifteen per cent.\nB: That is a strong line. Lead with it.\nA: I still feel like an outsider.\nB: Having taught for twelve years, you are not an outsider. You are experienced in the hard part.\nA: The hard part being the teaching itself?\nB: Yes. Anyone can learn the industry words.",
