   "text": "A: There is a conference next month. I should probably go and network.\nB: You say that as if you are going to the dentist.\nA: I find it awkward. Everyone is selling something.\nB: Then do not do that version. Talk to three people properly.\nA: Only three?\nB: Three real conversations beat thirty cards.\nA: What do I even say?\nB: Ask what they are working on and what is difficult about it.\nA: And afterwards?\nB: Send one message the same week. Reference something they said.\nA: Asking for what?\nB: Nothing. That is the point.\nA: It feels strange to contact someone with no request.\nB: It feels strange because most people only get in touch when they need a favour.\nA: So the request comes later.\nB: Much later, if at all. And by then you are not a stranger.\nA: What if I have nothing useful to offer?\nB: You do. Introductions cost nothing and are remembered for years.",
