  "speaking": {
   "card": "Describe a project or task that you helped to organise. You should say: what the project was; who was involved; what your responsibilities were; and explain whether it was completed successfully.",
   "part3": "Why do so many large projects go over budget? / Should governments use private companies for public projects? / Is it better to plan in detail or to stay flexible? / How do teams recover from a serious delay?",
   "useful": "The main risk at this stage is / We are currently on track to / That would push the deadline back by / Before we commit to a date / Once the approval comes through"
  },
  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Large public projects such as railways and hospitals are often delayed and cost far more than planned. What are the causes, and what could be done to improve the situation?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，说明问题普遍存在并预告结构",
    "主体一：原因——最初预算为争取批准而低估、范围变更、审批与协调复杂",
    "主体二：对策——独立成本评估、分阶段批准、变更须公开定价与问责",
    "结论：透明的估算与问责机制比更多规划文件更有效"
   ],
   "model": "Major public projects are notorious for finishing late and costing far more than the figure originally announced. Both the causes and the possible remedies are reasonably well understood.\n\nThe first cause is political rather than technical. Initial budgets are often deliberately optimistic, because a realistic figure might prevent the project from being approved at all. Once construction has begun, cancellation becomes politically impossible, so extra funding is granted repeatedly. Genuine complexity adds to the problem, as large schemes involve many contractors, changing regulations and requirements that are altered years after the design was agreed.\n\nSeveral measures could improve matters. Cost estimates should be produced by independent bodies rather than by those promoting the scheme, and funding could be released in stages, with each stage depending on an honest review of the last. Any change to the agreed scope should be published together with its cost, so that the public can see who requested it and why.\n\nIn my view, transparency matters more than additional planning documents. When decisions and their consequences are visible, the incentive to promise impossible figures largely disappears.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 原因与对策两部分都完整回答",
    "✔ 每段有清晰主题句",
    "✔ 时间状语从句使用正确（until / once / before）",
    "✔ 使用 in my view 等表达个人判断",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，结论呼应题目"
   ]
  },
