   "text": "A: I have been assigned a mentor at work. We meet monthly.\nB: How are the meetings going?\nA: We mostly talk about the weather and my current projects.\nB: So they are updates, not mentoring.\nA: I never know what to ask.\nB: That is the whole problem. Bring one real question.\nA: Such as?\nB: Something you are actually stuck on this week.\nA: I have been offered a transfer and I cannot decide.\nB: Perfect. Take that.\nA: It feels like wasting her time with my problems.\nB: Her time is being wasted now, talking about the weather.\nA: Fair. I wish I had done this from the start.\nB: You have not lost much. And ask her something else too.\nA: What?\nB: Whether she knows anyone doing the job you are considering.\nA: An introduction, you mean.\nB: Yes. Advice is useful, but an introduction is worth more.",
