  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that universities should focus on preparing students for employment, while others believe their purpose is to provide education for its own sake. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.",
   "outline": [
    "开头：改写题目，指出两种大学定位之争",
    "主体一：就业导向的理由——学费高昂、学生负债、雇主抱怨技能缺口",
    "主体二：通识教育的理由——培养思维与公民素养、职业会变、知识不可预测其用处",
    "结论：核心应是可迁移的思维能力，同时嵌入实习与实践机会"
   ],
   "model": "As tuition fees rise, universities are increasingly asked whether their purpose is to produce employable graduates or educated citizens. Both arguments deserve attention.\n\nThose who favour employment preparation point to cost. Students now borrow large sums, and it seems reasonable that a degree should improve their prospects. Employers also complain that graduates arrive without practical abilities such as writing clear reports or working in a team, and courses that include placements demonstrably improve the chances of finding work.\n\nThe opposing view is that education has value beyond the labour market. Universities exist to develop analytical thinking, independent judgement and knowledge that may have no obvious application for decades. Furthermore, since many of today's occupations will disappear, training students for current jobs may prepare them for a world that no longer exists by the time they graduate.\n\nIn my opinion, the distinction is largely false. The abilities that make someone employable over a whole career, such as reasoning from evidence and communicating clearly, are precisely those a good education develops. Universities should therefore continue to teach subjects seriously, while offering placements so that students can practise applying what they know.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 两种观点各一段并有具体理由",
    "✔ 结论提出个人立场并调和两者",
    "✔ 连接词使用多样且标点正确（furthermore / therefore）",
    "✔ 语域正式，无口语缩写",
    "✔ 词数 150-200，紧扣题目"
   ]
  },
