   "text": "A: You have been to about twenty countries. Which cuisine impressed you most?\nB: Vietnamese, without any doubt. Everything tasted fresh and light.\nA: Really? I expected you to say Italian or Japanese.\nB: I love those too, but Vietnamese food surprised me. The herbs completely changed the flavour.\nA: Was it very different from the Vietnamese restaurants here?\nB: Totally. The portions were smaller and the soup was much less sweet.\nA: So the food we get here is not authentic?\nB: It is adapted. Restaurants adjust the seasoning for local customers.\nA: That makes sense. Did you learn to cook anything?\nB: One noodle soup, from scratch. It takes six hours, so I only make it for special occasions.",
