   "text": "A: Why do you always refuse the tea at my office?\nB: Because you make it with boiling water. Green tea should never be steeped like that.\nA: I had no idea. Is that why it tastes bitter?\nB: Exactly. Eighty degrees is enough, and two minutes is plenty.\nA: You sound like my grandmother. She has a whole ritual every morning.\nB: Most tea drinkers do. Mine takes about five minutes and I quite enjoy it.\nA: Five minutes just for a drink? I would rather use a machine.\nB: That is the point, though. It forces me to slow down before work.\nA: All right, teach me. I will buy proper leaves this weekend.\nB: Good. Bring them in on Monday and we will brew a pot together.",
