  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people prefer to visit many different places on holiday, while others prefer to stay in one place for a longer time. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.",
   "outline": [
    "首段：介绍两种旅行方式，说明将讨论双方",
    "主体段1：多地旅行——见识广、适合首次到访、性价比高",
    "主体段2：久居一地——深入了解文化、更放松、支持当地",
    "结论：个人偏好久居一地，但取决于时间与目的"
   ],
   "model": "When planning a holiday, some travellers try to see as many places as possible, while others prefer to remain in a single destination. Both approaches have clear benefits.\n\nVisiting several places has obvious appeal. Travellers can compare different regions, see famous landmarks and decide which areas they might return to later. For someone visiting a country for the first time, or for a short period, a varied itinerary may offer better value.\n\nStaying in one place, however, allows a much deeper experience. After several days, visitors begin to understand local routines, meet the same shopkeepers and learn a few words of the language. The holiday also becomes more relaxing, since no time is wasted on stations and airports, and the money spent stays within one community.\n\nIn my opinion, the second approach is more rewarding. Although I enjoy seeing new cities, my strongest memories come from the towns where I stayed long enough to feel almost at home.",
   "checklist": [
    "首段介绍双方并保持中立",
    "两个主体段分别论述，长度大致平衡",
    "结论清楚给出个人观点并简要说明理由",
    "至少使用两个定语从句（who / which）",
    "检查主谓一致与时态统一"
   ]
  },
