   "model": "Alcohol advertising is tightly controlled in several countries, and I believe such restrictions are justified, though a total ban would be excessive.\n\nThe strongest argument for restriction concerns young people. Advertisements typically associate drinking with friendship, success and attractive lifestyles, and adolescents are especially influenced by these images. Since alcohol contributes to accidents, violence and long-term illness, reducing exposure is a reasonable public health measure.\n\nOn the other hand, alcohol remains a legal product, and producers employ large numbers of people and pay considerable taxes. Prohibiting all advertising would give an unfair advantage to established brands, whose names are already familiar, and would do nothing to address the social causes of heavy drinking. Education has been shown to change behaviour more effectively than censorship.\n\nIn my view, the sensible solution lies between the two positions. Advertising should be banned around schools and during programmes watched by children, and health warnings should be compulsory, while responsible advertising to adults remains permitted.",
   "checklist": [
    "首段给出有条件的立场",
    "两个主体段论据充分且互相制衡",
    "至少使用两组形容词顺序正确的短语",
    "结论提出具体的折中做法",
    "避免绝对化措辞"
   ]
