  "speaking": {
   "card": "Describe a mealtime custom in your country. You should say: what the custom is; when it happens; who takes part; and explain how you feel about it.",
   "part3": "Why do eating customs differ so much between countries? / Are family meals less common than in the past? / What can visitors do to avoid causing offence at the table? / How has eating out changed family life?",
   "useful": "It is customary to wait for the host / Dishes are placed in the middle and shared / We used to eat together every evening / I am still getting used to eating so late / Leaving a little food is considered polite"
  },
  "writing": {
   "prompt": "In many countries, families eat together less often than in the past. What are the causes of this change, and what effects does it have?",
   "outline": [
    "首段：改写题目，说明将分析原因与影响",
    "主体段1：原因——工作时间不规律、通勤、课外活动、外卖与屏幕",
    "主体段2：影响——沟通减少、饮食质量下降、儿童社交学习受损",
    "结论：总结并提出每周固定共餐的建议"
   ],
   "model": "In many households, the shared evening meal has become an occasional event rather than a daily routine. This change has several causes and a number of significant effects.\n\nThe main cause is the modern timetable. Parents work irregular or long hours and commute considerable distances, while children attend clubs and extra classes, so the household is rarely at home at the same time. Convenience food and delivery services have removed the practical need to cook, and televisions and phones make it easy to eat separately.\n\nThe effects are more serious than they first appear. Families lose their most dependable opportunity for conversation, which particularly affects teenagers, who may go days without discussing anything important with a parent. Diet also suffers, because meals eaten alone are more likely to be processed. Children, moreover, learn table manners and conversation skills by observing adults.\n\nIn conclusion, busy schedules and convenient food have reduced shared meals, weakening communication and nutrition. Even two or three fixed family meals each week would help considerably.",
   "checklist": [
    "首段说明文章结构（原因+影响）",
    "原因段与影响段清晰分开",
    "使用 used to 或 be used to 至少一次",
    "结论提出务实建议",
    "词数 150–200"
   ]
  },
