   "text": "A: I could not understand a word your uncle said at lunch.\nB: He was speaking dialect. Even I only catch about eighty per cent.\nA: Is it really that different from the standard language?\nB: Completely. Different vocabulary, different pronunciation, sometimes different grammar.\nA: Did you speak it as a child?\nB: My parents told me it would hold me back at school, so they spoke standard at home.\nA: Do you regret that?\nB: I do now. I asked my mother why she made that decision and she said everyone did it then.\nA: Could you still learn it?\nB: I am trying. I told my uncle to speak only dialect to me, which is exhausting but effective.",
