  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that money spent on public art would be better spent on practical improvements such as roads and housing. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "首段：改写题目并表明立场（不同意，主张平衡）",
    "主体段1：让步——住房与基础设施确实更紧迫",
    "主体段2：反驳——公共艺术成本低、改善环境、带动旅游与社区认同",
    "结论：两者预算规模不可比，不应对立"
   ],
   "model": "It is often argued that public money spent on murals and sculptures would be better used repairing roads or building homes. Although I understand this reasoning, I do not entirely agree.\n\nThere is clearly a case for prioritising infrastructure. Families waiting for housing or commuters using damaged roads have urgent, measurable needs, and it is difficult to justify a sculpture to someone living in temporary accommodation. In times of economic difficulty, cultural budgets are understandably questioned.\n\nNevertheless, the sums involved are rarely comparable. Public art typically represents a tiny fraction of a city budget, and removing it would not fund a housing programme. Well-chosen artworks also produce practical benefits: neglected areas look cared for, vandalism often falls, and visitors are attracted to districts that were previously ignored. A city that functions but offers nothing to look at is not a city people want to live in.\n\nIn conclusion, despite the pressure on public finances, I believe modest investment in public art is justified, provided that essential services are properly funded first.",
   "checklist": [
    "首段表明立场并承认对方逻辑",
    "让步段真诚具体",
    "至少使用 although 与 despite 各一次",
    "反驳段包含预算规模的论证",
    "结论加上优先级条件"
   ]
  },
