  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe that tourists should be restricted from photographing local people and religious places. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "首段：改写题目并表明立场（部分同意）",
    "主体段1：同意——宗教场所与私人生活应受保护，摄影可造成不适与不尊重",
    "主体段2：不同意——全面限制难以执行，摄影有记录与交流价值",
    "结论：以明确标识、许可制度与教育代替一刀切禁令"
   ],
   "model": "Whether tourists should be prevented from photographing residents and sacred sites is an increasingly common question. I partly agree with such restrictions, though a general ban would be impractical.\n\nThere are strong reasons to limit photography in certain places. Religious buildings are used for worship, not sightseeing, and flashing cameras during a ceremony are plainly disrespectful. Residents of heavily visited neighbourhoods also complain that they are photographed constantly while going about ordinary business, which few people would tolerate at home.\n\nHowever, prohibiting photography entirely would be difficult to enforce and would remove genuine benefits. Images taken by visitors document traditions, support local tourism and often create understanding between cultures. Many communities are happy to be photographed when they are asked politely, and a rule treating every tourist as intrusive ignores this.\n\nIn my view, clear signs, restricted areas within religious sites and better information for visitors would solve most problems. Educating tourists to ask permission is more realistic, and more respectful, than an outright ban.",
   "checklist": [
    "首段表明部分同意的立场",
    "宗教场所与普通居民分开讨论",
    "至少使用两个分词短语结构",
    "提出可执行的替代方案",
    "结论呼应立场并给出理由"
   ]
  },
