   "text": "A: Why do you go all the way across town for vegetables?\nB: Because a lot of the produce there was picked the same morning.\nA: Is it not more expensive?\nB: Cheaper, actually, if you go after two. They knock the price down to clear the stall.\nA: I never know whether I am supposed to haggle.\nB: Not for food. For secondhand things, yes, a little.\nA: How much can you knock off?\nB: Ten or twenty per cent, if you are polite about it. Each of the stallholders is different.\nA: And you actually enjoy it?\nB: I do. I have been going for six years, and none of the supermarkets can compete on flavour.",
