   "text": "A: I keep arriving at work with no memory of the journey.\nB: Classic autopilot. Your body drives while your head is at the office.\nA: Should I be worried?\nB: Not worried, but you had better build in one conscious moment.\nA: Such as?\nB: Before you start the car, take three breaths and notice your hands on the wheel.\nA: That sounds too simple to matter.\nB: It is simple, not easy. Try it for a week.\nA: What if my mind keeps jumping to my emails?\nB: Then you notice that, name it, and come back. That is the whole practice.\nA: No app required?\nB: None. You ought to start with something you already do every day.",
