  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think employers must provide ergonomic equipment for all staff. Others believe workers should take responsibility for their own health at work. Discuss both views and give your opinion.",
   "outline": [
    "引入：久坐相关病假上升",
    "雇主责任：工作条件由公司决定、设备成本低于病假损失",
    "个人责任：习惯与休息由员工掌控、设备无法替代活动",
    "立场：雇主提供基本设备与休息制度，员工负责使用"
   ],
   "model": "Back and neck problems are among the most common reasons for sick leave, so who should pay for prevention is a practical question.\n\nThe argument for employer responsibility is straightforward. Companies decide what desks, chairs and screens are available, and the cost of a monitor stand is trivial compared with weeks of absence. Since the workplace creates the risk, it seems reasonable that the workplace reduces it, just as it provides safety equipment in a factory.\n\nOthers reply that equipment alone changes nothing. Research suggests that the biggest factor is how long people stay still, and no employer can force staff to stand up every hour. Workers who ignore breaks and hunch over phones during lunch will suffer regardless of what they sit on.\n\nI would argue that responsibility is genuinely shared, but the two parties control different things. Employers should supply adjustable equipment and, more importantly, a culture in which leaving the desk is normal rather than suspicious. Employees must then use those breaks. Without both, the money spent on ergonomic furniture will simply buy a more comfortable form of immobility.",
   "checklist": [
    "双方论点是否明确区分控制范围",
    "动名词与不定式搭配是否正确",
    "主题词汇：ergonomic, slouch, strain, immobility",
    "结论强调共同责任并具体化",
    "字数 150-200，语言自然"
   ]
  },
