   "text": "A: How is the ankle? You have been out for a month.\nB: Better, but slower than I hoped.\nA: When will you play again?\nB: Not until the physiotherapist agrees. Probably another six weeks.\nA: Six? It looks fine to me.\nB: It looks fine because the swelling has gone. The strength has not come back.\nA: What are you doing meanwhile?\nB: Balance work every morning, and cycling instead of running.\nA: That must be frustrating.\nB: It was, until I accepted the timeline. Now I just tick off the exercises.\nA: Sensible. My cousin came back early and tore it again.\nB: Exactly. As soon as you rush, you go backwards.",
