   "text": "A: My doctor told me to spend more time outside. Literally wrote it down.\nB: A green prescription. They are becoming common.\nA: I thought she was being dismissive.\nB: Did she explain why?\nA: She said two hours a week made a measurable difference.\nB: That matches the research. It does not have to be countryside either.\nA: There is a park ten minutes away, though I never use it.\nB: Start with lunchtimes. Twenty minutes counts.\nA: Is walking necessary, or can I just sit?\nB: Sitting is fine. She probably meant exposure, not exercise.\nA: That sounds manageable.\nB: Try it for a fortnight and see whether you sleep better.",
