   "text": "A: My hospital offers an art group on Thursdays. I felt embarrassed even asking.\nB: Why embarrassed?\nA: Because I cannot draw. I have not drawn since primary school.\nB: That is true of almost everyone. It is not an art class.\nA: What actually happens?\nB: You choose materials and make something for forty minutes. Nobody comments.\nA: Does the therapist explain what it means?\nB: No. She asks what you notice about it. The meaning is yours.\nA: That sounds less frightening than talking.\nB: For many people it is. There is no performance.\nA: I might go next week.\nB: Take an old shirt. The paint gets everywhere.",
