   "text": "A: My mother has joined a dance therapy group at the health centre.\nB: Is that for her Parkinson's?\nA: Partly. Her walking is steadier when there is music.\nB: I have read about that. Rhythm helps with movement.\nA: The strange part is how much she talks about it.\nB: What happens in the sessions?\nA: They walk around the room, then copy each other's movements in pairs.\nB: That sounds odd on paper.\nA: It does, but she comes home brighter than after physiotherapy.\nB: Maybe it is the company as much as the dancing.\nA: Probably both. She goes on Wednesdays at two.\nB: Whatever works. She is eighty-one and dancing.",
