   "text": "A: My blood test showed low vitamin D. I was surprised.\nB: Honestly, half the country is low in winter.\nA: But I walk to work every day.\nB: It does not matter here. The sun is too weak from October.\nA: So what am I supposed to do?\nB: Take a supplement until spring. They cost a few pounds.\nA: Is that all? No special diet?\nB: Oily fish and eggs help a little, but you cannot eat enough to fix it.\nA: Will it stop me feeling tired?\nB: Possibly not. Fatigue has many causes, so do not expect a miracle.\nA: Fair enough. And in summer?\nB: Ten minutes of sun on your arms, then sunscreen. That is the balance.",
