   "text": "A: My uncle has started leaving one field empty every year. Isn't that a waste?\nB: Not really. He's probably resting the soil so it stays fertile.\nA: Doesn't he lose money on that field?\nB: For one season, yes. But the next crop is usually stronger.\nA: I suppose the soil needs time to recover, like anything else.\nB: Exactly. He's also planted a hedge to stop erosion on the slope.\nA: Does it work? The rain washes everything down there.\nB: It does. The roots hold the soil, and the bees love the flowers.\nA: If more farmers did that, would it really make a difference?\nB: Across a whole valley, absolutely. Small changes add up quickly.",
