   "text": "A: There's a waiting list for the allotments behind the station. Four years!\nB: That long? I had no idea they were so popular.\nA: Apparently applications doubled during the pandemic and never went back down.\nB: What would you even grow? It sounds like a lot of work.\nA: Beans, potatoes, tomatoes. My grandmother did it all her life.\nB: I'd probably kill everything. I've never had green fingers.\nA: Nobody does at first. There's usually someone who'll show you.\nB: That's the appealing bit, actually. You'd meet the neighbours properly.\nA: Exactly. Half the people there go for the conversation, not the vegetables.\nB: Put my name down too, then. In four years I might be ready.",
