   "text": "A: Look at those tracks by the river. Something big walked through here.\nB: They must be deer. There's a herd in the woods behind the farm.\nA: Could they be wild boar? I heard they've come back to this valley.\nB: They might have. A farmer told me he lost half a field last month.\nA: That must be frustrating. Does he get any compensation?\nB: A little, from the council, but it doesn't cover everything.\nA: No wonder some farmers want them shot.\nB: I understand it. Although the boar can't have caused all that damage alone.\nA: True. Deer probably did some of it.\nB: Either way, someone has to pay if we want them here.",
