  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe that environmental problems are too complex for ordinary citizens to understand, so decisions should be left to experts. To what extent do you agree or disagree? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "Intro: 改写题目并表明部分同意但反对完全交给专家。",
    "Body 1: 专家的作用 - 科学判断需要专业训练与数据。",
    "Body 2: 但决策包含价值取舍 - 谁承担成本、如何分配，属于公共问题。",
    "结论: 专家提供事实，公民决定优先级，需加强公共科学教育。"
   ],
   "model": "Environmental science involves complicated data, and it is sometimes argued that policy should therefore be determined by specialists rather than by public debate. I partly agree, but I believe this position confuses two different kinds of question.\n\nExperts are clearly indispensable for factual judgements. Determining how quickly ice sheets are melting or how much nitrogen a river can absorb requires years of training and access to long-term data. When such questions are decided by popular opinion or political convenience, the results are usually poor, as the long delay in acting on tobacco and lead pollution demonstrated. Scientific advice should certainly be independent and clearly communicated.\n\nHowever, most environmental decisions are not purely technical. Choosing between a flood defence that protects a wealthy district and one that protects a poorer neighbourhood is a question of fairness, not hydrology. Deciding how much present consumption to sacrifice for future generations involves values that no measurement can settle. In a democracy, such trade-offs must be made by citizens through their representatives, and policies imposed by unelected specialists tend to attract resentment and quiet non-compliance.\n\nIn conclusion, I believe experts should define the range of realistic options and explain their consequences, while the public decides which option to accept. This requires far better science education and honest communication, so that citizens can engage with evidence rather than being asked either to obey it or to ignore it.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 首段改写题目并区分两类问题",
    "✔ 支持专家的段落给出历史例证",
    "✔ 反驳段说明价值判断属于公共领域",
    "✔ 使用 however, in conclusion 等连接词",
    "✔ 结论提出专家与公众的分工"
   ]
  },
