   "text": "A: Our office doesn't buy printers any more. We lease them.\nB: Does that actually save money?\nA: About the same, but the supplier maintains them and takes them back.\nB: So they have a reason to send you a machine that doesn't break.\nA: Exactly. When the contract ends, they refurbish it and lease it again.\nB: That's smarter than selling something cheap and disposable.\nA: It is. Although we're locked into a five-year agreement.\nB: That's the trade-off. Are the cartridges included?\nA: Yes, and they collect the empty ones. Nothing goes in the bin.\nB: I'll suggest it to my manager. It sounds sensible for laptops too.",
