   "text": "A: They're knocking down the old library to build an eco-centre.\nB: That seems contradictory. The library was perfectly solid.\nA: The council says the new building will be carbon neutral in use.\nB: Yes, but demolition itself produces enormous emissions.\nA: How long would it take to break even?\nB: For a sound building? Often forty or fifty years.\nA: So retrofitting would have been better?\nB: Almost certainly. Thicker insulation, new windows, a heat pump.\nA: I suppose a retrofit doesn't look impressive in a press photo.\nB: Exactly. That's half the reason these decisions get made.",
