   "text": "A: Do you buy organic? The apples are almost double the price.\nB: Only some things. Milk and eggs, mainly, because of animal welfare.\nA: Not fruit and vegetables?\nB: Not usually. The nutritional difference is pretty small, from what I've read.\nA: What about pesticide residues? That's why my mother buys organic.\nB: They are lower, that's true. Washing removes most of it though.\nA: So is organic farming better for the environment or not?\nB: On the field itself, definitely. More insects, better soil.\nA: But?\nB: But yields are lower, so you need more land. It's a real trade-off.",
