   "x": "must 通常表示说话人自己认为的强烈必要，如 I must leave by six；have to 更多表示外部规定或客观要求，如 I have to attend the meeting（公司要求）。should 表示建议或应该，语气较弱，如 You should set clearer boundaries。be supposed to 表示按规定或按预期应该做，常暗示实际没做到，如 We are supposed to finish at five, but we never do。特别注意 mustn't 表示「禁止」，而 don't have to 表示「不必」，两者意思完全不同：You mustn't answer emails at midnight（禁止）vs You don't have to answer emails at midnight（不必）。",
