  "writing": {
   "prompt": "In many countries, employees are expected to answer work messages outside office hours. Do the advantages of this flexibility outweigh the disadvantages? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目并表明弊大于利。",
    "主体1：优点——紧急问题可快速解决，工作时间更灵活。",
    "主体2：缺点——休息被侵占、长期压力、家庭时间减少。",
    "结论：应通过明确规则划定界限，如非紧急不联系。"
   ],
   "model": "In many workplaces, staff are now expected to reply to messages long after they have left the office. Although this brings some flexibility, I believe the disadvantages are greater.\n\nThere are certainly benefits. Urgent problems can be solved immediately, which matters in international teams working across time zones. Employees who answer a message in the evening may also be allowed to arrive later the next morning, and this arrangement suits some families.\n\nThe costs, however, are serious. When work can reach us at any moment, rest is never complete, and the mind stays half prepared for the next request. Over time this produces exhaustion and poor sleep, which harms both health and the quality of the work itself. Family time also suffers, since a five-minute reply often turns into an hour.\n\nIn my view, the solution is not to ban technology but to agree clear limits. If companies define what counts as urgent and respect quiet hours, flexibility can survive without destroying personal time.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 首段改写题目并给出总体判断",
    "✔ 一段写优点、一段写缺点，结构平衡",
    "✔ 使用具体细节（时区、睡眠、家庭时间）",
    "✔ 使用 however, in my view 等衔接",
    "✔ 结论提出可行建议并呼应立场"
   ]
  },
