   "text": "A: Did you notice how quiet you went when your dad criticised the food?\nB: I always do that. It's a habit from childhood.\nA: What happened at home if you argued back?\nB: Nothing dramatic. My parents just stopped talking for a day, so I learned to stay silent.\nA: That explains a lot about our arguments, actually.\nB: I know. Silence feels safe to me, but I realise it feels like punishment to you.\nA: It does. I'd honestly rather have a loud ten minutes than a quiet evening.\nB: I'm trying to change it. Last week I actually said I was annoyed.\nA: You did, and the world didn't end.\nB: No, it didn't. Old patterns are hard to break, but not impossible.",
