   "prompt": "Some people say that online communication has made friendships weaker, while others believe it helps people stay close. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目，说明双方观点与自己的立场。",
    "主体1：削弱的一面——点赞代替真实交流，联系人多但深度不足。",
    "主体2：加强的一面——跨国、跨时区保持联系，重逢门槛降低。",
    "结论：技术是工具，效果取决于使用方式。"
   ],
   "model": "Opinions differ on whether digital communication has weakened or strengthened friendship. In my view, technology itself is neutral, and the outcome depends on how it is used.\n\nCritics make a reasonable point. Liking a photograph takes two seconds and creates the comfortable illusion of contact, so weeks pass without a real conversation. Some people now have hundreds of online contacts but nobody they would call at midnight, and this shallow breadth can replace genuine depth.\n\nSupporters, however, note advantages that did not exist a generation ago. Friends separated by thousands of kilometres can share daily details through voice messages, which keeps the relationship alive until they meet again. Group chats also make it far easier to organise a reunion than a chain of phone calls ever did.\n\nOverall, I believe online tools maintain friendships well but rarely deepen them. Used to arrange real meetings and to send small personal messages, they are valuable; used only for public posting, they slowly replace friendship with performance.",
