   "prompt": "Some people believe that experiencing failure is necessary for personal growth. To what extent do you agree or disagree? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目并表明大体同意。",
    "主体1：失败带来的收获——具体反馈、抗压能力、对成功的现实认知。",
    "主体2：限定条件——失败必须可承受且有支持，否则会造成长期伤害。",
    "结论：有支持的、可控范围内的失败才有价值。"
   ],
   "model": "It is widely claimed that failure is essential for personal development. I largely agree, although I believe this is only true under certain conditions.\n\nFailure provides information that success cannot. A student who receives a poor mark learns exactly which parts of the subject were misunderstood, while a good mark simply confirms that something worked. Repeated small failures also reduce the fear of trying, because each recovery is evidence that a bad week eventually ends.\n\nHowever, the benefit disappears when the failure is too large or the person is unsupported. Someone who loses their home or their health does not become stronger automatically; they may become exhausted and afraid. In education, the same applies: a child who fails constantly without help concludes that effort is pointless rather than that methods can change.\n\nIn conclusion, I agree that failure contributes to growth, but only when it is survivable and accompanied by guidance. What teaches us is not the failure itself, but the recovery that follows it.",
