  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that employers should train staff in communication and empathy, while others believe these skills cannot be taught. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目并给出立场（可以训练，但需持续练习）。",
    "主体1：可训练的一面——具体行为如复述、提问、暂缓建议。",
    "主体2：怀疑者的理由——态度难以强迫，一次培训效果有限。",
    "结论：培训应聚焦可观察的行为并由管理者示范。"
   ],
   "model": "Opinions vary on whether communication and empathy can be developed through training at work. In my view, the underlying behaviours can certainly be taught, even if genuine concern cannot be ordered.\n\nThose who support training have practical evidence on their side. Empathy in the workplace consists largely of observable actions: asking a question before offering a solution, repeating back what has been heard, and checking whether advice is wanted. Medical schools have taught these techniques for years, and patients report clear improvements in how they are treated.\n\nSceptics reply that attitudes cannot be installed in a one-day course, and this is fair. Staff who feel rushed and unsupported will not suddenly become patient listeners because of a workshop, and forced exercises can feel artificial.\n\nMy own conclusion is that training works when it focuses on specific habits and when managers demonstrate them daily. Skills improve through repetition, not inspiration, so a short course followed by consistent example will change a workplace far more than an emotional speech.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 首段改写题目并表明立场",
    "✔ 分别陈述支持与怀疑两种观点",
    "✔ 举出具体可观察的行为作为例证",
    "✔ 使用 my own conclusion is 等表达个人观点",
    "✔ 结尾提出条件性结论，不引入新论点"
   ]
  },
