   "text": "A: You've mentioned your grandmother three times today.\nB: I know. I keep thinking I should have visited her more last year.\nA: You were working two jobs and living in another city.\nB: That's what everyone says. It doesn't stop me feeling awful.\nA: Did she ever complain about it?\nB: Never. She used to tell me not to waste money on train tickets.\nA: So the standard you're judging yourself by isn't even hers.\nB: No, I suppose it isn't. I wish I had called more often, though.\nA: Then call your mother tonight. You can't repair the past, only the present.\nB: That's true. I'll ring her after dinner.",
