   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目，指出两派观点并给出立场（取决于是否有具体行动）。",
    "主体1：有益的一面——促成道歉、修复关系、维持社会规范。",
    "主体2：有害的一面——过度内疚导致回避、失眠、以不切实际标准自责。",
    "结论：能带来修复行动的内疚有用，反复自责则无益。"
   ],
   "model": "People disagree about whether guilt is a helpful emotion. In my opinion, its value depends entirely on whether it leads to action.\n\nThose who defend guilt have a strong argument. It appears when we break our own rules and pushes us to repair the damage, for example by apologising to a colleague we spoke to rudely. Without this signal, relationships would break down far more often, since nobody would feel any pressure to correct their behaviour.\n\nCritics point out, however, that guilt frequently continues long after it is useful. Many working parents feel guilty every evening although their children are perfectly happy, simply because they compare themselves with an impossible ideal. This kind of guilt causes exhaustion and, ironically, makes people less patient with the very people they worry about.\n\nMy conclusion is that guilt should be judged by its results. When it produces an apology or a changed habit within a short time, it is doing its job. When it merely repeats in the mind for months, it has become self-punishment and should be replaced by a more realistic standard.",
