   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目并表明不同意。",
    "主体1：反驳——价值观的表达方式改变，而非消失；举透明度与环保为例。",
    "主体2：让步——流动性与匿名性确实削弱了某些形式的忠诚。",
    "结论：价值观在演变而非衰退。"
   ],
   "model": "It is often claimed that honesty and loyalty matter less to people today than they did in the past. I largely disagree, since I believe these values have changed form rather than disappeared.\n\nModern societies arguably demand more honesty, not less. Companies are now expected to publish their salaries, their suppliers and their environmental impact, and behaviour that was accepted fifty years ago frequently ends a career today. Younger employees also refuse to stay silent about unfair treatment, which requires considerable courage.\n\nThere is nevertheless a reasonable point behind the complaint. Loyalty to a single employer or a single neighbourhood has certainly declined, because people move far more often and few companies offer lifelong security in return. Online anonymity also allows behaviour that would be impossible face to face.\n\nIn conclusion, I would argue that traditional values are being expressed differently rather than abandoned. Loyalty is now directed towards people and causes instead of institutions, and honesty is demanded more publicly than ever before.",
