   "prompt": "Some people believe that social media has a negative effect on how young people see themselves. To what extent do you agree or disagree? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目并表明基本同意。",
    "主体1：负面影响——精选内容造成失真的正常标准、滤镜影响自我形象。",
    "主体2：让步——也提供社群支持与学习机会，效果因使用方式而异。",
    "结论：影响主要取决于使用方式与教育，需要媒体素养教育。"
   ],
   "model": "It is widely argued that social media harms the way young people view themselves. I broadly agree, although the effect depends heavily on how the platforms are used.\n\nThe main problem is distorted comparison. Feeds display carefully selected moments, so teenagers measure their ordinary daily lives against other people's best days. Editing tools make this worse: when almost every face has been quietly adjusted, an unedited appearance begins to feel abnormal, and research links heavy use to dissatisfaction with body image.\n\nIt would be unfair, however, to ignore the benefits. Young people with unusual interests or health conditions often find supportive communities that do not exist in their town, and many learn skills from creators who share their work openly.\n\nIn conclusion, I agree that social media frequently damages self-image, but I do not believe the technology alone is responsible. Teaching young people how content is produced and edited, and encouraging them to follow accounts that inform rather than impress, would reduce the harm considerably.",
