   "text": "A: You look tired. What have you been doing all morning?\nB: I signed up for a volunteer project at the community centre, and today was my first shift.\nA: Really? What kind of work is it?\nB: Mostly helping older residents with their phones and online forms. It's slower than I expected.\nA: But is it rewarding?\nB: Honestly, yes. One man had never sent a photo to his grandchildren before today.\nA: That's lovely. How much of a commitment is it?\nB: Two hours every Saturday for six months. They asked for that before they would train me.\nA: I've always wanted to lend a hand somewhere, but I worry I'd give up.\nB: Then start small. Even one morning a month makes a difference, and they're desperate to recruit people.",
