   "text": "A: How's your grandfather settling in since he moved closer to you?\nB: Better than I expected, although the first month was hard.\nA: Does he still live on his own?\nB: Yes, in a small flat. A carer who works for the council visits twice a week.\nA: Is that enough support?\nB: For now. The bigger issue is isolation, honestly. He used to chat to neighbours he'd known for forty years.\nA: Has he found anything locally?\nB: There's a lunch club whose members are mostly his age. He complained about it for a month and now he never misses it.\nA: That's a good sign. And how are you coping?\nB: It does put a strain on my weekends, but I'd rather look after him than worry from a distance.",
