   "text": "A: You grew up in a village, didn't you? Would you ever go back?\nB: Maybe. It depends. If the internet gets faster, I'll seriously consider it.\nA: Is it that bad?\nB: It drops out constantly. And the bus to town runs twice a day, so you're cut off without a car.\nA: What about work?\nB: That's the real question. Unless I can work remotely, there's nothing there for me.\nA: Are people moving away?\nB: Constantly. My old school had ninety pupils; now it has thirty. If it falls below twenty, it will close.\nA: That's sad. Something must be done.\nB: If the council invests in broadband and keeps the clinic open, some families will stay. Otherwise the village will just fade away.",
