   "text": "A: Did you see the report on school funding this morning?\nB: I did. Apparently some schools spend twice as much per pupil as others.\nA: That can't be right in a state system.\nB: It happens through donations, mostly. If parents were less wealthy, those schools couldn't raise the extra money.\nA: So the gap isn't really about the government at all?\nB: Partly it is. Rural schools also struggle to recruit qualified teachers, so posts stay empty for months.\nA: What would you change, if you had the power?\nB: I'd allocate more funding to disadvantaged areas and pay teachers extra to work there.\nA: Wouldn't parents in richer areas object?\nB: Probably. But if every child had a decent library and a science lab, the whole country would benefit.",
