   "text": "A: How is your Spanish class going? You said it was difficult at first.\nB: It is, but I've improved. My teacher told me I had made real progress this term.\nA: That's encouraging. Are the others in the class local?\nB: No, mostly newcomers like me. One woman was a pharmacist back home.\nA: Is she working in a pharmacy here?\nB: Not yet. They told her that her qualifications weren't recognised, so she's studying again.\nA: That seems such a waste.\nB: It is. She asked the office whether there was a shorter conversion course, and they said there wasn't one in this region.\nA: Do you feel more settled these days?\nB: Slowly. Joining the football team helped more than anything. That's where I started to feel at home.",
