   "text": "A: Are you going to the council meeting about the bus route?\nB: I ought to, but it's at two in the afternoon. I'd have to take unpaid leave.\nA: That's exactly why nobody turns up.\nB: I know. They must realise that working people can't attend.\nA: You could send a written comment instead.\nB: I did last time, and I got a standard reply three weeks later.\nA: Then we'd better organise something bigger. A petition, maybe.\nB: That might work. The last one got six thousand signatures and they had to debate it.\nA: So it's not completely hopeless.\nB: No. You just have to be persistent, and you shouldn't expect a quick answer.",
