   "text": "A: Have you seen what they're planning for the old brewery site?\nB: I saw the model in the library. Four hundred flats, apparently.\nA: How many of them will be affordable housing?\nB: Ten per cent, which depends on the final costs. It usually shrinks.\nA: That's the pattern everywhere. My sister was priced out of her street last year.\nB: The frustrating thing is that the design itself is quite good. Shops on the ground floor, flats above.\nA: Mixed-use, at least. Better than another office block.\nB: True. And they're preserving the brewery chimney, which people are attached to.\nA: A chimney doesn't help if nobody local can afford to live there.\nB: Exactly. Residents are protesting against the housing figures, not the architecture.",
