   "text": "A: You're late again. Was it the bus?\nB: It was. If they hadn't cut the 34, I'd have been here twenty minutes ago.\nA: They cut it? That was the only direct route from your estate.\nB: Exactly. Now I have to change twice, and the connection is unreliable.\nA: Couldn't you cycle?\nB: Not with the children. And there's no safe route along the main road.\nA: What about the fares? I heard they went up again.\nB: They did. Peak-time prices are the worst part. I start at seven, so I always pay the highest fare.\nA: That seems completely backwards.\nB: It is. If the council had consulted shift workers, they'd have designed it differently.",
