   "text": "A: Were you here during the flood last winter?\nB: I was. It was the speed of it that shocked everyone. The water rose in about an hour.\nA: Did you have any warning?\nB: A text message at six in the morning. That's what saved most of the ground-floor flats.\nA: Who helped you move things upstairs?\nB: The neighbours, mainly. It was two students from the top floor who carried my mother's furniture.\nA: And the emergency services?\nB: They came later and coordinated the shelter at the school. That part was well organised.\nA: How long did it take to get back to normal?\nB: Months. What really delayed us was the insurance, not the repairs.",
