   "text": "A: You've got a new dog! Where did she come from?\nB: The shelter. She was a stray, so she must have been living outside for months.\nA: Poor thing. Was she in bad condition?\nB: Quite thin. They'd already neutered her and treated her for fleas.\nA: You should have told me — I'd have come with you to collect her.\nB: I nearly did. Honestly, I needn't have worried about the paperwork; it took twenty minutes.\nA: Are you thinking of getting a second one?\nB: Not yet. Looking after one properly is enough for now.\nA: Fair enough. It's better than buying from a breeder, anyway.\nB: That's what convinced me. Someone must have abandoned her, and the shelter takes in forty animals a month.",
