   "text": "A: How long have you been on the allotment waiting list?\nB: Three years. By the time I get a plot, my children will have left home.\nA: That's ridiculous. Is there nothing closer?\nB: There's a community garden behind the flats. It's shared rather than individual plots.\nA: Isn't that better? You'd meet more people.\nB: It is, actually. I go on Saturdays, and while I'm weeding, half the street stops to chat.\nA: What do you grow?\nB: Beans, potatoes, far too many courgettes. We divide the harvest as soon as it's ready.\nA: Do you argue about the work?\nB: Sometimes. That's why we wrote rules when we started. Until you agree who waters in August, nothing runs smoothly.",
