  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Large music festivals bring economic benefits to a region, but they also create environmental and social problems. Do the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：承认双面性，表明总体利大于弊但需管理",
    "主体一：优势——旅游收入、就业、地方形象与文化生活",
    "主体二：劣势——垃圾、噪音、交通与临时物价上涨",
    "结论：通过押金制、公共交通与限量售票可保留优势"
   ],
   "model": "Every summer, quiet regions host festivals that attract tens of thousands of visitors. In my opinion the benefits are greater than the drawbacks, provided that events are properly regulated.\n\nEconomically, the argument is strong. Visitors spend money on transport, accommodation and food, which supports hotels, farms and small shops during a short but valuable season. Festivals also create temporary jobs for students and give unknown local musicians an audience they could never reach alone, improving the cultural image of the whole area.\n\nThe problems, however, are real. Camping sites are often left covered in plastic and abandoned equipment, traffic blocks narrow roads, and residents lose sleep for several nights. Prices in nearby shops sometimes rise unfairly during the event.\n\nThese difficulties are mostly manageable rather than unavoidable. Deposits on cups and tents encourage people to return them, shuttle buses reduce private cars, and limiting ticket numbers protects the site. Where councils and organisers cooperate in this way, a festival can enrich a community for a weekend without damaging it for a year, so I believe the advantages clearly outweigh the disadvantages.",
   "checklist": [
    "明确回答 outweigh 的问题，不只是罗列",
    "优势段与劣势段各有具体细节",
    "结尾提出解决办法并重申立场",
    "使用 provided that / however / where 等衔接手段",
    "将来时与情态动词使用得当，无拼写错误"
   ]
  },
