   "text": "A: How was your first pottery class?\nB: Wet, cold and completely humbling.\nA: Did you make anything?\nB: Two bowls collapsed. The third one survived.\nA: What was the hardest part?\nB: Centring the clay. You have to press hard but stay calm.\nA: When will you see the finished piece?\nB: In about six weeks. It is dried, fired, glazed, then fired again.\nA: Six weeks for one bowl?\nB: I know. But the colours are decided in the kiln, not by me.\nA: That would drive me mad.\nB: Strangely, it is relaxing. Nothing can be undone, so you stop worrying.",
