  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people argue that public money should be spent on hospitals and schools rather than on theatres, orchestras and museums. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：承认医疗教育优先，但反对完全取消艺术资助",
    "主体一：艺术投入占比极小，社会与经济回报明显",
    "主体二：文化机构服务教育、旅游与心理健康",
    "结论：不是二选一，应保持合理比例"
   ],
   "model": "Whenever budgets are discussed, cultural institutions are among the first targets. I agree that health and education must come first, but I disagree that arts funding should therefore disappear.\n\nThe main reason is proportion. In most countries, support for theatres, orchestras and museums is a tiny share of national spending, so closing them would barely affect hospital waiting lists. What would be lost, however, is considerable: venues that employ thousands, attract tourists and generate tax revenue.\n\nThere is also a social argument. Subsidised theatres run school programmes that reach children whose families could never buy a ticket, and museums provide free education for entire regions. Studies link arts participation to better mental health among older people, which reduces pressure on the health services critics wish to protect.\n\nNaturally, funding should be conditional. Institutions that receive public money ought to keep prices low, tour outside the capital and open their doors to local schools. Managed in this way, arts spending is not a competitor to hospitals and classrooms but a modest partner to them, and treating the choice as either one or the other seems to me a false economy.",
   "checklist": [
    "回应题目中的公共资金优先级问题",
    "有比例、就业、教育等具体论据",
    "至少一处现在完成进行时或完成时",
    "让步与反驳结构清晰",
    "字数合规，无主谓一致错误"
   ]
  },
