  "writing": {
   "prompt": "With the widespread use of computers and phones, some people believe handwriting is no longer an important skill. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：承认打字普及，但反对手写无用",
    "主体一：手写与记忆、思考的关系",
    "主体二：签名、笔记、艺术与个人表达仍需手写",
    "结论：手写不再是主要工具，但仍是重要能力"
   ],
   "model": "Most communication now happens through screens, and some observers conclude that teaching handwriting is a waste of classroom time. Although typing is clearly the dominant skill, I do not accept that handwriting has lost its importance.\n\nThe strongest argument concerns learning. Research repeatedly shows that students who take notes by hand remember more than those who type, because writing is slower and forces them to summarise rather than copy. Forming letters also supports early literacy, helping young children recognise the shapes they later read.\n\nIn addition, handwriting continues to serve practical and personal purposes. Signatures, forms, quick notes and exam papers all require it, and a handwritten card carries an emotional weight that a message never achieves. Beyond daily use, calligraphy has become a respected art form, which would be impossible if the skill disappeared from schools entirely.\n\nI therefore agree only with the weaker version of the statement: handwriting is no longer the main tool of communication, and children should not spend years perfecting decorative letters. Despite this shift, the ability to write clearly and comfortably by hand remains valuable for thinking, learning and expression, and abandoning it would cost far more than the lesson time it saves.",
   "checklist": [
    "立场分层清楚（部分同意）",
    "有研究与实际用途两类论据",
    "让步结构 Although / Despite 使用正确",
    "无 although...but 的中式错误",
    "字数 150-200，结论明确"
   ]
  },
