  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that art should always be beautiful, while others believe that its main purpose is to make people think. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.",
   "outline": [
    "开头：说明美与思考两种艺术目的",
    "主体一：美的价值——愉悦、技艺、公共空间",
    "主体二：思考的价值——批判、议题、社会讨论",
    "结论：两者并非对立，最好的作品先吸引再提问"
   ],
   "model": "People have argued for centuries about what art is for. One view holds that art should give pleasure through beauty; another insists that its real task is to provoke thought.\n\nThe traditional position is easy to sympathise with. A skilful landscape or a well-designed building improves daily life, and attractive public spaces are simply more pleasant to inhabit. Beauty also demonstrates craft, which took years to acquire and deserves respect, and many visitors go to galleries precisely to escape the ugliness of ordinary streets.\n\nThe opposing argument is that comfort is not enough. Works dealing with war, poverty or the environment are unpleasant to look at yet force audiences to confront what they would rather ignore. Collage artists, for example, place advertising beside images of waste so that viewers question what they consume, and such pieces start conversations that a pretty picture never could.\n\nIn my opinion these purposes are complementary rather than opposed. A work that is only shocking is quickly forgotten, while one that is only decorative says nothing at all. The pieces that last usually attract the eye first and then ask a difficult question, holding attention long enough for the idea to arrive.",
   "checklist": [
    "两种目的均有充分论证",
    "结论提出整合式观点",
    "使用 so that / so ... that 结构",
    "有具体艺术形式作为例证",
    "词汇多样，字数合规"
   ]
  },
