   "text": "A: My father has started an art group at the hospital.\nB: Is he enjoying it?\nA: Surprisingly, yes. He has never drawn anything in his life.\nB: Is it a therapy session or just an activity?\nA: A therapist runs it, but nobody talks about feelings directly.\nB: So what do they do?\nA: They draw, and then they talk about the drawing.\nB: That seems easier than being asked how you feel.\nA: That is exactly what he said. The paper does the talking.\nB: Has it changed anything?\nA: He sleeps better on those days. Small things.\nB: Small things count when someone is ill.",
