   "text": "A: I bought this embroidered scarf at the market. Is it real?\nB: Let me see. The stitching is machine-made on this edge.\nA: So it is a copy?\nB: Probably printed abroad. A hand-embroidered one costs four times that.\nA: I feel a bit cheated.\nB: Most tourists cannot tell. That is the problem.\nA: How would I find a genuine one?\nB: Buy from a cooperative, or directly from the maker online.\nA: Is the tradition dying out?\nB: In some villages, yes. Young people cannot live on it.\nA: That is sad. The patterns are beautiful.\nB: They are, but beauty passed down for free does not pay rent.",
