  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people believe that learning about art and culture is only useful for those who work in creative jobs. To what extent do you agree or disagree?",
   "outline": [
    "开头：反对这种狭隘看法",
    "主体一：审美与观察力影响各行各业的判断与沟通",
    "主体二：文化素养带来生活质量与理解他人的能力",
    "结论：创意工作者受益最直接，但价值远超职业范围"
   ],
   "model": "It is sometimes suggested that studying art and culture matters only to designers, musicians and other creative professionals. Having spent time on the subject myself, I strongly disagree with this narrow view.\n\nThe first objection concerns skills that transfer. Looking carefully at a painting trains attention to detail and to how small changes alter an overall impression, valuable to an engineer, a manager or a teacher. Moreover, discussing why a work succeeds develops the habit of justifying an opinion with evidence, which is useful in any profession.\n\nThe second objection is about life outside work. Someone who knows a little music, architecture or film experiences ordinary days differently: a city walk, a workplace or an evening film all become richer. Cultural knowledge also builds understanding of other societies, since a novel or a piece of folk art often explains a country better than statistics.\n\nI accept that professionals in creative industries need this knowledge most directly, and their training must go far deeper. Nevertheless, treating art as relevant only to them is like treating exercise as relevant only to athletes. The benefits are broadest precisely among people who will never make a living from it.",
   "checklist": [
    "立场坚定并有清楚理由",
    "含让步段承认专业人士需求更深",
    "混合时态运用自然一致",
    "衔接副词标点正确",
    "字数 150-200，收尾有力"
   ]
  },
