   "text": "A: I saw a documentary last night about creatures living near volcanic vents.\nB: The ones in complete darkness? They're extraordinary. No sunlight at all.\nA: So what do they actually eat?\nB: Chemicals. Bacteria turn the gases from the vents into food, and everything else feeds on them.\nA: That completely changes what I thought life needed.\nB: It changed what biologists thought too. Nobody expected it before the late seventies.\nA: Is anyone still exploring down there?\nB: Not as much as you'd think. Every trip costs a fortune, and the pressure destroys ordinary equipment.\nA: Which is why we know more about Mars, I suppose.\nB: Exactly. It's easier to photograph a planet than to reach the bottom of your own ocean.",
