   "prompt": "Plastic waste in the ocean has become a serious global problem. What are the main causes of this problem, and what measures could be taken to solve it? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目，指出海洋塑料污染的规模。",
    "主体一：原因——一次性包装泛滥、废物处理系统不足、河流将垃圾带入海洋。",
    "主体二：措施——限制一次性塑料、改善回收、企业押金制度与国际合作。",
    "结论：强调需要个人与政府同时行动。"
   ],
   "model": "Every year millions of tonnes of plastic enter the sea, and the problem is now visible on beaches worldwide. This essay will consider the main causes and suggest possible solutions.\n\nThe first cause is the sheer volume of single-use packaging. Bottles, bags and food containers are designed to be thrown away within minutes but survive for centuries. Secondly, many countries lack proper waste collection, so rubbish is left near rivers and is carried straight into the ocean during heavy rain. Fishing equipment that is lost or dumped at sea also contributes significantly.\n\nSeveral measures could reduce the damage. Governments should ban or tax the least necessary plastic items, as several countries have already done with plastic bags. Deposit schemes, in which customers pay a small extra amount and receive it back when returning a bottle, have proved highly effective. Manufacturers could also be required to use packaging that is genuinely recyclable, and international agreements are needed because currents carry waste across borders.\n\nIn conclusion, the crisis is caused mainly by disposable design and weak waste systems, and it can only be solved if governments, companies and consumers act together.",
