   "text": "A: My cousin keeps telling me that quantum physics proves anything is possible.\nB: That's a very popular misunderstanding. It actually proves the opposite.\nA: In what sense?\nB: The predictions are extremely precise. It's the most accurately tested theory we have.\nA: Then why does everyone describe it as weird?\nB: Because at tiny scales particles behave in ways that don't match our experience. A particle has no definite position until you measure it.\nA: If that happened to ordinary objects, life would be chaos.\nB: It would. Fortunately the effects vanish as things get bigger.\nA: So it's just a curiosity, then?\nB: Not at all. Your phone contains chips that only work because of it.",
