   "text": "A: I found a shell in a rock halfway up the mountain last weekend.\nB: That's not unusual, actually. Those rocks were an ancient seabed.\nA: At three thousand metres?\nB: The whole range was pushed up when two plates collided. It just took a very long time.\nA: How long are we talking about?\nB: Tens of millions of years. The continents still move about as fast as your fingernails grow.\nA: That sounds far too slow to matter.\nB: It does, until you multiply it. As the plates keep pushing, the mountains are still rising today.\nA: So the landscape isn't finished.\nB: Nothing ever is. We just live too briefly to notice.",
