   "text": "A: I bought a carbon fibre bike frame at the weekend. It weighs almost nothing.\nB: They're remarkable, aren't they? Stiffer than steel at a fraction of the weight.\nA: The shop said it would last a lifetime.\nB: It might, as long as you never crash. Carbon doesn't bend, it cracks.\nA: That's slightly worrying.\nB: It's manageable. Just have it checked if you ever come off badly.\nA: And what happens to it eventually?\nB: That's the awkward part. The fibres are set in resin, so it can't really be separated or recycled.\nA: Whereas an aluminium frame could be melted down.\nB: Endlessly, more or less. It's heavier, but it comes back as something else.",
