   "text": "A: I did one of those home DNA tests. Apparently I have a variant linked to heart disease.\nB: That sounds alarming written down. What was the actual number?\nA: It said my risk was raised by about twenty per cent.\nB: Twenty per cent of what, though? If the base risk is two per cent, that takes you to two point four.\nA: The report didn't put it that way at all.\nB: They rarely do. A relative increase always sounds bigger than it is.\nA: So should I ignore it?\nB: Not ignore it. Mention it to your doctor. But the advice will probably be the same as for everyone else.\nA: Exercise, sleep, less salt.\nB: Exactly. Although it is worth knowing whether it runs in your family.",
