  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Genetic testing allows people to learn about diseases they may develop in the future. Do the advantages of this outweigh the disadvantages? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "引言：改写题目，说明基因检测普及化。",
    "主体一：优势——早期筛查、生活方式调整、家庭规划与心理准备。",
    "主体二：劣势——焦虑、误读概率、保险与就业歧视风险。",
    "结论：在有专业解读与法律保护的前提下优势更大。"
   ],
   "model": "Tests that reveal a person's risk of future illness are now widely available, and opinions about their value are divided. In my view the advantages are greater, but only where results are properly explained and legally protected.\n\nThe benefits are real. Someone who learns of a raised risk of bowel cancer can begin screening a decade earlier than normal, and early detection dramatically improves survival. Such knowledge can also motivate changes in diet and exercise that people had previously postponed, and it allows families to plan sensibly for conditions that may affect children.\n\nNevertheless, the drawbacks deserve attention. Many reports present relative risks that sound frightening but change very little in absolute terms, and anxiety about an illness that never develops carries its own health cost. There is also a serious risk of discrimination if insurers or employers gain access to this information.\n\nThese problems, however, can largely be managed. Several countries already prohibit the use of genetic data in insurance decisions, and results delivered through a doctor rather than an app are far less likely to be misread.\n\nOverall, I believe genetic testing offers genuine medical value, provided that interpretation is professional and privacy is guaranteed by law.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 首段直接回答 advantages outweigh 的问题",
    "✔ 优势与劣势各成一段并有例子",
    "✔ 有一段回应劣势，体现思辨",
    "✔ 使用 nevertheless, however, overall 等衔接",
    "✔ 结论与首段立场一致"
   ]
  },
