   "text": "A: I've applied to work at a research station in Antarctica for the winter.\nB: Seriously? Six months of darkness with the same twelve people.\nA: That's the part everyone mentions. I keep telling them the cold doesn't worry me.\nB: The cold isn't the problem. You're indoors most of the time.\nA: So what is?\nB: Boredom, mainly. And the fact that you can't leave, even if something goes wrong at home.\nA: They asked about that in the interview, actually. Half the questions were about conflict.\nB: That doesn't surprise me. They're selecting for temperament, not fitness.\nA: I suppose I'll find out whether I have any.\nB: You'll come back either very calm or very talkative.",
