   "text": "A: My cousin lives about fifteen kilometres from an active volcano. I find that terrifying.\nB: It sounds worse than it is, honestly. Most of those areas are monitored constantly.\nA: But if it erupts, fifteen kilometres is nothing.\nB: It depends what comes out. Lava flows are usually slow. Ash and sudden collapses are the real danger.\nA: Then why does anyone stay?\nB: The soil, mainly. It's some of the most fertile farmland in the world.\nA: That seems like a strange trade.\nB: It's a calculated one. An eruption might come once a century; the harvest comes every year.\nA: I suppose they get warnings now, at least.\nB: Usually weeks in advance. The hard part is convincing people to actually leave.",
