   "text": "A: I saw a photograph of the glacier above my grandmother's village taken in 1920. It reached the valley floor.\nB: And now?\nA: It stops about a kilometre up the mountain. You can see the bare rock where it used to be.\nB: That's happening almost everywhere. The odd thing is that the river below has actually been fuller recently.\nA: That doesn't make sense to me.\nB: It does temporarily. Melting ice releases extra water for a few decades.\nA: So the river is being fed by the glacier disappearing.\nB: Precisely. And when the ice is gone, the summer flow will drop very suddenly.\nA: The farmers must know that.\nB: Some do. But it's hard to plan for a problem that currently looks like good news.",
