   "text": "A: I went out to look at the stars last night and honestly saw about five.\nB: How long did you stay outside?\nA: A couple of minutes. It was freezing.\nB: That's the problem, then. Your eyes need twenty minutes to adjust properly.\nA: Twenty? I had no idea.\nB: And don't look at your phone while you wait. One glance undoes the whole thing.\nA: I definitely did that.\nB: Try again on a clear night, take a warm coat and a red torch if you have one.\nA: What should I actually look at?\nB: Start with the Moon and Jupiter. They're bright enough to see from a city, and Jupiter's moons move night by night.",
