   "text": "A: I watched the landing broadcast last night. Everyone in the control room looked terrified.\nB: They usually are. Those seven minutes are completely out of their hands.\nA: Because of the signal delay?\nB: Exactly. By the time they hear that the parachute has opened, the craft has already landed or crashed.\nA: That must be unbearable.\nB: It is. And roughly half of all landing attempts have failed.\nA: I hadn't realised it was that bad.\nB: Mars is awkward. There's enough atmosphere to burn you up, but not enough to slow you down.\nA: So how do they manage it at all?\nB: A combination of heat shields, parachutes and rockets, all timed automatically. Nothing is controlled from Earth.",
