   "text": "A: We're thinking about putting solar panels on the roof, but my father says they never pay for themselves.\nB: That was true fifteen years ago. Prices have fallen by about ninety per cent since then.\nA: Ninety? That can't be right.\nB: It is, and hardly anyone predicted it. The early subsidies get criticised, but they created the market that brought costs down.\nA: What about cloudy days, though? We're not exactly in a sunny country.\nB: You generate less, obviously, but panels still work in diffuse light. The bigger issue is what happens in the evening.\nA: When we actually use electricity.\nB: Exactly. That's why people add a battery, though it does increase the cost considerably.\nA: So is it worth it or not?\nB: On most roofs, yes, over about eight years. Get two quotes and compare them carefully.",
