   "text": "A: I read that people who drink coffee live longer. I'm taking that as permission.\nB: Was it a study of coffee drinkers, or an experiment?\nA: What's the difference?\nB: A study just observes. Coffee drinkers might be wealthier, or more social, or younger on average.\nA: So the coffee might have nothing to do with it.\nB: It might not. That's the correlation problem. Two things rise together without one causing the other.\nA: How would you ever prove it, then?\nB: You'd need to assign people randomly to drink coffee or not, which is difficult and expensive.\nA: I preferred the headline.\nB: Most people do. But a single study rarely means much until someone repeats it.",
