   "text": "A: You look busy. What are you writing?\nB: My goals for the next three months. I'm trying to be more realistic this time.\nA: What went wrong last time?\nB: I wrote things like \"become fluent in English\". It sounds great, but I never knew what to do on Monday morning.\nA: So how are you changing it?\nB: I'm breaking it down. Ten new words a day, one conversation class a week, and one article every weekend.\nA: That sounds achievable. Are you going to track it somewhere?\nB: Yes, in a paper notebook. I like ticking boxes — it feels like real progress.\nA: Good idea. What's your deadline?\nB: The end of June. I'm taking the test in July, so I can't fall behind.",
