   "text": "A: You've been getting up early for weeks now. How do you do it?\nB: Honestly, I stopped relying on willpower. I just made the habit smaller.\nA: Smaller? I thought the point was to push yourself.\nB: Not at the start. I began with five minutes of reading, not an hour.\nA: And that was enough?\nB: It was enough to keep the streak going. Now it's about forty minutes, but it happened gradually.\nA: What stops you from slipping back into old routines?\nB: The trigger. I always read while the kettle boils, so the kettle reminds me.\nA: Clever. Do you reward yourself?\nB: Just a tick on the calendar. It sounds childish, but seeing thirty ticks really works.",
