   "text": "A: Can I ask you something about the meeting yesterday? It overran by an hour.\nB: I know. I'm sorry — the discussion was going well and I didn't want to cut it off.\nA: That's the thing. For me, a two o'clock meeting ends at three.\nB: Fair enough. Where I grew up, finishing a conversation matters more than the clock.\nA: I've never thought about it that way, to be honest.\nB: Neither did I until I moved here. People looked annoyed and I couldn't work out why.\nA: So how do we handle the next one?\nB: Let's agree in advance. A hard stop at three, and anything unfinished goes to email.\nA: Perfect. I'm always pressed for time on Thursdays.\nB: Then Thursday meetings will be short. I promise.",
