  "writing": {
   "prompt": "Some people think that advertising encourages consumers to buy things they do not really need, and that it should be more strictly controlled. To what extent do you agree or disagree? (250 words)",
   "outline": [
    "Intro: paraphrase and agree with limits, especially for vulnerable groups.",
    "Body 1: advertising does create artificial needs and exploits psychology.",
    "Body 2: it also informs consumers and funds free services, so a total ban is unrealistic.",
    "Conclusion: targeted regulation rather than blanket restriction."
   ],
   "model": "It is often claimed that advertising persuades people to buy unnecessary products and should therefore face tighter rules. I broadly agree, although I believe regulation should be targeted rather than total.\n\nThere is clear evidence that advertising manufactures desire. Campaigns rarely describe what a product does; instead they connect it with status, romance or belonging. Techniques such as countdown timers and \"was–now\" pricing exploit well-documented weaknesses in human judgement, and children are particularly easy to influence because they cannot recognise persuasion.\n\nHowever, advertising also performs useful functions. Consumers cannot compare products they have never heard of, and small businesses depend on advertising to reach customers at all. Much of the free content people enjoy online is funded in the same way. A complete ban would protect nobody and would simply favour companies that are already famous.\n\nFor this reason, I support specific restrictions rather than sweeping ones. Marketing junk food to young children could be prohibited, misleading discount claims could be fined, and gambling advertisements could be limited, while ordinary product information remains free.\n\nIn conclusion, advertising deserves stricter control where it exploits vulnerable groups or misleads deliberately, but the aim should be honesty rather than silence.",
   "checklist": [
    "✔ 首段改写题目并给出限定立场",
    "✔ 正反两面各成一段",
    "✔ 具体例子（倒计时/原价现价/儿童广告）",
    "✔ 使用 however, for this reason, in conclusion 衔接",
    "✔ 结论提出可操作的监管方向"
   ]
  },
