   "text": "A: I've signed up for a statistics course. I'm slightly regretting it.\nB: Why? You're good with numbers.\nA: That's the thing — I've said \"I'm not a numbers person\" since school.\nB: And is it true?\nA: Apparently not. I got the hang of the first module in a fortnight.\nB: So what's the problem?\nA: Looking stupid in front of people ten years younger than me.\nB: Everyone feels that. Although it's uncomfortable, it passes after a few weeks.\nA: I hope so. My colleague retrained completely at forty-five.\nB: Exactly. Confidence comes after competence, not before it.",
